        "original_id": "433c3fdb-55f9-5926-bd2c-a5fc09d6ae99",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Donaldson, André Cayatte, Chris Donaldson\n- Roles: film director, producer, writer, filmmaker, lawyer\n- Films: Smash Palace, No Way Out, Dante's Peak, Thirteen Days, The World's Fastest Indian\n- Topics: crime, justice, moral responsibility, family relationships\n\nFacts:\n- André Cayatte was born on 3 February 1909 in Carcassonne and died on 6 February 1989 in Paris.\n- André Cayatte was a French filmmaker and lawyer known for films about crime, justice, and moral responsibility.\n- Roger Donaldson was born on 15 November 1945.\n- Roger Donaldson is an Australian-born New Zealand film director, producer, and writer.\n- Roger Donaldson directed the acclaimed 1981 relationship drama \"Smash Palace\".\n- Roger Donaldson directed the Kevin Costner film \"No Way Out\" in 1987.\n- Roger Donaldson directed the disaster film \"Dante's Peak\" in 1997.\n- Roger Donaldson directed the Kevin Costner film \"Thirteen Days\" in 2000.\n- Roger Donaldson's films include \"The World's Fastest Indian\" from 2005.\n- Chris Donaldson is the son of film director Roger Donaldson.",
